    "title": "Local McDonald's locations to distribute free backpacks - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Natalie St. Denis ,\n1 hours ago\nRelated video: Watervliet graduating seniors receive free laptops\nALBANY, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — While summer isn’t over yet, back-to-school time is just around the corner and local McDonald’s locations around the Capital Region are helping families prepare for the return to the classroom. The Golden Arches Pack Giveback Program will provide free backpacks for students in need.\nDownload our WTEN+ streaming app on Roku, Fire TV and Apple TV! Now in it’s second year , the program allows McDonald’s owners and operators across New York State to distribute backpacks. Each bag will be filled with essential school supplies.\nOn August 5, from 4 p.m. to 6 p.m., the following locations will be participating in the giveaway:\n391 Central Ave. in Albany 1006 Central Ave. in Albany 31 Holland Ave. in Albany 1224 State St. in Schenectady 10 Trieble Ave. in Ballston Spa 1 Park Plaza in Mechanicville 3632 Main St. in Warrensburg 7621 NY-32 in Cairo 2939 US Highway 9 in Valatie 55 Maple Ave. (Route 9W) in Catskill 12187 State Route 9W in West Coxsackie 8644 State Highway 22 in Granville Get the latest news, weather, sports and entertainment delivered right to your inbox! Backpacks are available while supplies last. Each student is limited to one bag and they must be present to receive it. For more information and to see the full statewide list of participating McDonald’s locations, visit the program’s website .\nFor more news on school districts, make sure to check out the Classroom Progress Report category under the NEWS tab on the NEWS10 website.\nRead the latest from NEWS10:\nNEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader!\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.\n1",
    "summary": "By Natalie St. Denis , Related video: Watervliet graduating seniors receive free laptops ALBANY, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — While summer isn’t over yet, back-to-school time is just around the corner and local McDonald’s locations around the Capital Region are helping families prepare for the return to the classroom. The Golden Arches Pack Giveback Program will provide free backpacks for students in need. Now in it’s second year , the program allows McDonald’s owners and operators across New York State to distribute backpacks.",
